      "id": "origins-earth-human-history-s023-p00268",
      "source_en": "It is astonishing that the vast majority of the large animals that we domesticated over the last 10,000 years, and which human civilisation came to depend upon for their meat, secondary products and muscle power, are all members of just one group of mammals. But there's something equally fascinating and profound about how these ungulates first emerged.",
